Third-party material
====================

The manuals and datasheets in this directory are not part of this
project, and the project's license does not apply to them.  Each is
the property of its copyright holder.  They are included for reference
because they are the specification this project is written against:
`PLAN.md` and the code cite them by document and section.

No license to any of this material is granted or implied by its
presence here.

Motorola
--------

In `motorola/`.  Motorola's semiconductor manuals, later published by
Freescale and then NXP.  NXP no longer serves them at the addresses
below.  Copied from the m683xx-emu project's `third_party/`, whose
NOTICE gives their provenance: the reference manuals are NXP's own
files as archived by the Internet Archive (web.archive.org) on
2019-08-21; the user's manual came from the smartclock project's
`third_party/` (github.com/charlieh0tel/smartclock).

  CPU32RM.pdf      "CPU32 Central Processor Unit Reference Manual",
                   (c) Motorola 1990, 1996.  nxp.com/docs/en/
                   reference-manual/CPU32RM.pdf.  Authoritative for
                   background debug mode (7.2): its serial interface
                   and timing (7.2.7) and command set and encodings
                   (7.2.8).  Its RSREG format figure (7.2.8.6) is a
                   misprint (PLAN.md, Protocol summary).
                   SHA-256 4a096e7edfbc01086dff56ca76677e8c
                           c4281ec53d7e86bfc2a3c98df9505916
  MC68331UM.pdf    "MC68331 User's Manual", (c) Motorola 1996;
                   (c) Freescale Semiconductor, Inc., 2004.
                   nxp.com/docs/en/data-sheet/MC68331UM.pdf.  The
                   target: BDM summary (5.10.2), the BDM connector
                   (Figure 5-11), BDM timing (Table A-7), the SIM and
                   reset configuration.
                   SHA-256 d5d71f87309b4d8d5a5af76b9bff79ed
                           82b3a58dd697f513ebeedca9f1ec17eb
  SIMRM.pdf        "System Integration Module Reference Manual",
                   Motorola.  The file prints no copyright notice or
                   year; its PDF metadata gives it to Freescale
                   Semiconductor, Inc., made 1997-08-14 and last
                   changed 2004-05-04.
                   nxp.com/docs/en/reference-manual/SIMRM.pdf.  Reset
                   timing, chip selects and the rest of the SIM, for
                   the target init script.
                   SHA-256 bf8ed68d5e07e8e4f0972d1c3e175fdf
                           43e837f99264bf4e524616c3edb0ef70

